<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en-AU">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>Register | Intelligent Talent Matching Platform</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Choose whether to register for TalentMatch as a candidate or an employer." />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/lib/css/font-awesome.min.css" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/lib/css/modern-normalize.min.css" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/global.css" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/register.css" />
    <script src="/lib/js/jquery.min.js"></script>
</head>
<body class="<%= theme === 'DARK' ? 'dark-mode' : '' %>">
<%- include('../partials/public-header/public-header'); %>
<main class="register-landing">
    <section class="register-landing__hero" aria-labelledby="register-landing-title">
        <img class="register-landing__hero-image" src="/images/register/register-hero.jpg" alt="Professional using a laptop in a modern office" />
        <div class="register-landing__hero-overlay"></div>
        <div class="register-landing__hero-inner">
            <p class="register-landing__eyebrow">
                Create your account
            </p>
            <h1 id="register-landing-title" class="register-landing__title">
                Start on the side of TalentMatch that fits what you need.
            </h1>
            <p class="register-landing__description">
                Candidates use TalentMatch to build a profile and find relevant roles.
                Employers use it to represent an organisation and find people worth speaking to.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="register-landing__intro" aria-label="Choose a registration path">
        <p>
            You can change how you use TalentMatch later if your workflow grows.
            For now, choose the path that matches the account you need to create.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="register-landing__path register-landing__path--candidate" aria-labelledby="register-candidate-title">
        <div class="register-landing__path-media">
            <img src="/images/home/hero-candidate.png" alt="Candidate reviewing job opportunities" />
        </div>
        <div class="register-landing__path-copy">
            <p class="register-landing__eyebrow">
                Candidate
            </p>
            <h2 id="register-candidate-title">
                Set up the account TalentMatch will use to understand your next move.
            </h2>
            <p>
                Candidate registration starts with the practical details that shape matching:
                what you do, where you want to work, how you want to work, and what kind
                of roles are worth showing you.
            </p>
            <ul class="register-landing__list">
                <li>Add the profile details needed for role matching.</li>
                <li>Set work preferences before browsing opportunities.</li>
                <li>Use one candidate sign-in for saved roles and applications.</li>
            </ul>
            <a class="register-landing__path-action" href="/candidate/register">
                Register as a candidate
            </a>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="register-landing__path register-landing__path--employer" aria-labelledby="register-employer-title">
        <div class="register-landing__path-media">
            <img src="/images/home/hero-employer.png" alt="Employer reviewing candidate matches" />
        </div>
        <div class="register-landing__path-copy">
            <p class="register-landing__eyebrow">
                Employer
            </p>
            <h2 id="register-employer-title">
                Create the employer access your team needs before posting or searching.
            </h2>
            <p>
                Employer registration is for people acting on behalf of an organisation.
                It prepares the company side of TalentMatch so jobs, hiring activity,
                and candidate discovery sit under the right business profile.
            </p>
            <ul class="register-landing__list">
                <li>Connect your account to an organisation profile.</li>
                <li>Prepare company details before creating hiring activity.</li>
                <li>Keep employer tools separate from candidate-only workflows.</li>
            </ul>
            <a class="register-landing__path-action" href="/employer/register">
                Register as an employer
            </a>
        </div>
    </section>
</main>
<%- include('../partials/footer/footer'); %>
<script src="/js/global.js"></script>
<script src="/js/register.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
